WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.186 --> 00:00:04.930
♪ [music)] ♪

00:00:06.036 --> 00:00:08.598
Give me one minute
and I'll show you how Composer

00:00:08.598 --> 00:00:11.450
can help you automate
your workflows quickly.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:14.351
Cloud Composer is a managed
Apache Airflow service

00:00:14.351 --> 00:00:18.650
that helps you create, schedule, monitor
and manage workflows.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.269
Composer workflows
can connect data processing and services

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:26.317
in Google Cloud, other public clouds
and on premise environments.

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.523
Because it is built upon
open-source Apache Airflow,

00:00:29.523 --> 00:00:32.813
users are free from lock-in and benefit
from the communities' active

00:00:32.813 --> 00:00:35.646
and rich library
of connectors and plugins.

00:00:35.646 --> 00:00:37.771
Interacting with Composer is easy.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:41.205
You can user the Cloud Console,
GCloud command line tool,

00:00:41.205 --> 00:00:44.479
or user the API
with client libraries of your choice.

00:00:44.479 --> 00:00:48.028
Start by creating a composer environment
where you configure your pipeline

00:00:48.028 --> 00:00:50.325
with directed acyclic graphs.

00:00:50.325 --> 00:00:54.323
A dag defines the tasks and dependencies
that are part of your workflow

00:00:54.323 --> 00:00:56.466
and is written using Python.

00:00:56.466 --> 00:01:01.690
Deploy your workflow and then monitor it
in the Airflow UI and in Cloud monitoring.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.346
Use Composer to orchestrate
your ETL pipelines that process data

00:01:05.346 --> 00:01:07.736
in your data warehouse and data lake.

00:01:07.736 --> 00:01:11.374
Or, use it to automate analytics
and machine learning jobs.

00:01:11.374 --> 00:01:14.588
So next time you're looking to configure
and orchestrate workflows,

00:01:14.588 --> 00:01:16.613
take a minute to look at Composer.

00:01:18.674 --> 00:01:22.844
To learn more,
checkout cloud.google.com/composer.

